# DEPLOY-HARDEN-1 — Immutable Deployment Entrypoint & Self-Update Safety

Verified by `php artisan foundation:deployment-entrypoint-check --strict`
(rules **DH1-R001..R012**) and `tests/Feature/Deploy/DeployHarden*Test.php`.

## The invariant

```
RUNNING_DEPLOY_PROGRAM != MUTABLE_REPOSITORY_FILE
```

bash reads a script incrementally and keeps a byte offset into the open file. A
deployment that rewrites its own script mid-run is undefined behaviour. This is
not theoretical: it cost two production releases a manual pre-pull rescue.

## Permanent rules

1. A running deployment program must never execute from a repository file that
   can be rewritten during that same deployment.
2. Deploy and rollback execute from an **immutable trusted snapshot** created by
   `scripts/deploy-immutable-exec.sh` before any mutation.
3. The snapshot is exported from a git **object** (`git archive`), never copied
   from the working tree.
4. Every script executed across the repository mutation belongs to the snapshot
   closure. Never `source` or `bash` a helper out of the working tree after the
   checkout — that is the same defect one indirection removed.
5. The live `deploy/runtime-identity.conf` is overlaid onto the snapshot: rolling
   the CODE back must never roll the RUNTIME IDENTITY back (INFRA-SEC-RUNTIME-1).
6. The deployment target is pinned to an **exact SHA** before any mutation. A
   remote branch that moves afterwards belongs to a LATER deployment.
7. `git merge --ff-only "$TARGET_SHA"`, never `git pull` of a moving tip.
8. HEAD is verified against the pinned target after the checkout **and** as the
   last gate before `DEPLOY OK`.
9. Exactly one deployment critical section at a time: `flock` on
   `/run/daengtisiams-deploy/<role>.lock`. A second attempt fails closed (exit
   75) before backup, migration or checkout.
10. Lock and snapshot live under a root-controlled path — **never** under
    `storage/` or `bootstrap/cache`, which the runtime user can write.
11. The advisory lock is authoritative. A lock file on disk, or a stale status
    file, is not. Never delete a lock file to unstick a deploy.
12. Cleanup is trap-driven and guarded (`rm -rf` only on this run's own snapshot,
    real directory, no symlink) and never rewrites the exit code.
13. Backup still runs **before** migration; backup failure aborts the deploy.
14. `migrate --force` only. Never a destructive database command.
15. A dirty tracked production checkout fails closed. Never `git reset --hard`,
    never discard production work to make a deploy pass.
16. `scripts/deploy-vps-runner.sh` runs **on the production VPS only** — never
    locally, never on a CI runner, never in a worktree.
17. Launcher start is not deployment completion. `exit=0` **and** the `DEPLOY OK`
    marker are the authority.
18. **A manual pre-pull is never a prerequisite.** If a change reintroduces one,
    that is a NO-GO — the core defect is back.
19. Production deploys only merged release authority, never an unmerged
    candidate SHA.
20. Rollback obeys all of the above and resolves the operator's tag to one exact
    commit before mutating; its snapshot comes from the CURRENT code so the
    modern security gates still run against an older target.
21. Deployment scripts never print a secret value.
22. Every new deployment-architecture test must belong to an authoritative CI
    gate — the `DeployHarden` token in the NSF-R011 critical filter (both the
    GitHub-hosted and the self-hosted variant).

## Adding to the deployment path

- Put contract literals in `config/deployment_entrypoint.php`, not in the shell
  scripts or the scanner (ENT-9/ENT-10/ENT-11 config-not-code convention).
- A new helper invoked after the checkout must be added to
  `execution_closure.closure_members` and called via `${DEPLOY_TOOLS_DIR}`.
- Re-run `foundation:deployment-entrypoint-check --strict`,
  `foundation:deployment-rollback-check`, `foundation:cicd-enterprise-gate-check`
  and the `DeployHarden` suite before proposing a change.
